Negative control for the SORT-COMES-FROM-THE-SORT-ENUM law (`R6-28`).

Offers the schema's FILTER columns as the ordering vocabulary instead of its own
`sort` enum — the two lists overlap on one field and disagree on the rest, which
is exactly the second-source-of-truth the ruling killed. Every `order=` the
control then writes names a column the API does not order on.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the table-channel spec — `declared().sort` is the query schema's own sort
enum, field for field and in its order.

